<!--
  BlockML Definition — root block definition meta-model type

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.definition.RootBlockDefinition
  Describes the parse-time shape of root <block> documents.
  See docs/12_bom_object_model.md — BlockDefinition.
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:bml="http://blockml.org/schema/bml">

  <idea>The structural shape of root Block definition documents in BlockML.</idea>

  <documentation>Meta-model type for root block documents. Extends
    org.blockml.bml.definition.SubBlockDefinition with the definition property and the
    embeddedBlocks aggregation for inline Block documents under the root block of a BomDocument.
    subBlocks is inherited from SubBlockDefinition.

    The definition property (inherited from SubBlockDefinition, overridden here for root blocks
    and embedded blocks) selects which Definition meta-model type shapes this Block's definition
    document. Default when &lt;definition&gt; is omitted: org.blockml.bml.definition.RootBlockDefinition
    for document root blocks and embedded blocks. Sub-Blocks default to
    org.blockml.bml.definition.SubBlockDefinition instead (see SubBlockDefinition).

    embeddedBlocks holds an Inline Library — inline definitions of additional Block documents
    within the same BomDocument. Each embedded block is structurally a full root block: own FQN,
    members, subBlocks, and nested embeddedBlocks. Think of embeddedBlocks as a library
    co-located within a single Block: multiple BML files in one source document, including Blocks
    from packages that do not belong to the root block's package. Each embedded block's FQN is the
    fully qualified value of its mandatory &lt;type&gt; element. Sub-Blocks on an embedded block
    derive their FQNs from the embedded block's type. Within this document's resolution scope, an
    embedded definition and all its descendants shadow the corresponding library or file-based
    BlockDefinition; externally they remain invisible.</documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="12_bom_object_model.md">
      BlockDefinition BOM structure.
    </see>
    <see file="02_mbml.md">
      Block definition authoring format and Sub-Block rules.
    </see>
    <see block="def:SubBlockDefinition">
      Shared block definition shape — identity, members, and metadata.
    </see>
  </references>

  <name>RootBlockDefinition</name>
  <type>def:RootBlockDefinition</type>
  <baseType>def:SubBlockDefinition</baseType>

  <properties>
    <definition type="FullyQualifiedName(def:RootBlockDefinition)">
      <value>def:RootBlockDefinition</value>
      <documentation>Definition meta-model type for this Block's definition document (root block
        and embedded blocks). Selects which fields exist when accessing the definition via bml:Self
        in definition reflection — for example com.foo.Bar.idea or additional properties on a custom
        definition model. Omitted on root blocks and embedded blocks =
        org.blockml.bml.definition.RootBlockDefinition.

        Authored as FQN, xmlns QName, or unqualified name — unqualified names at this site resolve
        via implicit namespace org.blockml.bml.definition.* (for example RootBlockDefinition or
        definition:RootBlockDefinition). The referenced type must extend
        org.blockml.bml.definition.RootBlockDefinition (BML_DEFINITION_TYPE_MISMATCH when declared
        on a Sub-Block or when the type does not extend RootBlockDefinition). Addressable as
        com.foo.Bar.definition.</documentation>
    </definition>
  </properties>

  <aggregations>
    <embeddedBlocks type="def:RootBlockDefinition[]">
      <documentation>Inline Library — inline Block definitions embedded in this BomDocument (root
        block and embedded blocks only — forbidden on Sub-Blocks, BML_EMBEDDED_BLOCKS_ON_SUBBLOCK).
        Gedankenstütze: embeddedBlocks is a library co-located within a single Block document —
        multiple BML files in one source file, including Blocks from packages outside the root
        block's namespace. Each entry is a full RootBlockDefinition with a mandatory, fully
        qualified &lt;type&gt; (BML_MISSING_EMBEDDED_BLOCK_TYPE,
        BML_UNQUALIFIED_EMBEDDED_BLOCK_TYPE). The embedded block's FQN is exactly resolve(type) —
        not nested under the enclosing block's FQN (for example com.foo.internal.Physics, not
        com.foo.Vehicle.embeddedBlocks.com.foo.internal.Physics). Sub-Blocks on an embedded block
        derive their FQNs from the embedded block's type. Embedded blocks may declare their own
        subBlocks and embeddedBlocks. Within this document, the embedded definition and all
        descendants shadow the corresponding library or file-based BlockDefinition; externally
        they remain invisible. Composition references from within this document must use the fully
        qualified Block type. Addressable as com.foo.internal.Physics.* (canonical paths of the
        embedded Block itself).</documentation>
    </embeddedBlocks>
  </aggregations>
</block>
